    "disposition": [
      "Final sema issues immutable owner/type/reachability proofs; global and closed RuntimePlan scopes use the same RuntimeExecutableTypeProjection algebra. Separate owned expression, pattern, local and annotation type catalogs were removed. Temporary validation maps only borrow that authority.",
      "Source local order is validated before filtering semantic locals from the runtime frame. Semantic aliases never acquire Unit types, Core callable identities or local storage. Global generic-local context stays on the same typed projection.",
      "One typed expression-evaluation map distinguishes runtime operands from completed semantic prefixes. Flow continuations execute initializer, callee and argument prefixes in source order exactly once, close lexical scopes, and resume without manufacturing a runtime operand.",
      "The existing Compiler and RuntimePlan owners retain projection/admission/continuation responsibilities. Their large-file triggers require ownership review; no source-name scan, I/O, renderer owner, legacy reader, contract version or Cargo edge was introduced."
    ]
  },
  "corrections": [
    "The old Source 3f7f1108f9ec96d2950085c943d224fea6315e91 Flow failure was real. After global type projection was repaired, the same case reached Flow binding and exposed a missing local seed; that intermediate 1/1 FAIL is retained.",
    "The compile-only regression was replaced by six actual Native/decoded AWBC Flow execution cases. The final five-target integration run includes all 18 View cases and passes all 292 cases with no exclusions.",
    "The new test helper initially used the wrong plan ownership API and then captured a consuming restore in FnMut; all three compiler failures remain in owner1/2/3 catalogs. The fixed helper preserves one-op/max_ops=1/256 ticks and performs public save/owned restore after every AWBC step.",
    "The first library catalog and a later check exposed direct mutations of deleted private type tables and missing test imports. They were migrated without dropping rejection assertions. The final four-library run passes 2621 cases, with 8 ignored and the existing HIR limit test still slow."
  ],
  "remaining": [
